{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes","id":1049778,"title":"Cheating Rotes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-16T03:31:59-08:00","id":1049778,"title":"Cheating Rotes","content":"Cleverness is often more important for a Mage than Power, so hear are a few Rotes I've bean using for the past quarter century with grate effect. I'll post a few over the next couple of days as I dig out some old character sheets and find them, for starters<br /> <br /> Like a Ton of Bricks (Mater 2, Forces 2)<br /> Instead of trying to deliver direct damage to a target the Mage weakens the structural integrity of a nearby building (or the one they are in) and brings a section of wall or ceiling down on the target, Mater is used to transmute the materiel (mortar in brick work, support beams ect) and Forces to direct the falling debris. the coincidence is practically built in to the Rote be it poor workmanship, dodgy materials or deterioration due to age and/or environmental effects.<br /> <br /> being indirect damage unless they are very careful the player is giving up direct control over what happens, but it can easily be potentially more than they could be capable of using a direct attack (a pane of toughened glass from ten stories up, or a literal ton of bricks has more damage potential than a four dice fireball, but not a panel of quarter inch think brick facade held in place by render, perspex skylight or gyprock floating ceiling).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T04:20:15-08:00","id":1049784,"title":"","content":"Power Sink<br /> (Mind 2, Prime 2)<br /> Sometimes it is enough to appear powerful...<br /> To this end this rote gives some unidentifiable power to your aura for others to notice.<br /> <br /> Related is the \u201cfailure\u201c to hide the power you posess. A short slip in the veil you constructed to hide your terrifying might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:54:09-08:00","id":1049936,"title":"","content":"That Ton of Bricks rote is really overpowered as it can potentially do a lot more damage than a direct effect rote unless you require a large number of successes. It also handwaves away a bunch of stuff like buildings actually being really difficult to demolish.<br /> <br /> There's a very similar example on p440 of the M20 rules where an <b>Enlightenment 7</b> character knocks down a pillar with a similar strength as a brick wall, but that example has six successes going for it. A rote like this that needs to do major damage to a building should need a minimum of 4 or more successes to work (4 successes +1 for forces = 10 health levels vs durability 4 structure 6 brick walls)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:17:09-08:00","id":1049982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1049936#post1049936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Ton of Bricks rote is really overpowered as it can potentially do a lot more damage than a direct effect rote unless you require a large number of successes. It also handwaves away a bunch of stuff like buildings actually being really difficult to demolish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not go throwing around the word &quot;Overpowered&quot;, willy nilly. For one thing, it's only Coincidental if the building is obviously in disrepair or of obviously poor quality. That makes the Rote situational (assuming you want to avoid Paradox). You also need a building over one's head or a brick wall at your side for it to work. Say what you want about the fireball's vulgarity, at least you can use it anywhere.<br /> <br /> You know what else a fireball does better than falling rubble? Aggravated damage. Because it's fire. Falling bricks would be Bashing, which can potentially be soaked.<br /> <br /> Oh! And there's the fact that, when you go around compromising the roof over your head, <i>you are compromising the roof over your head</i>. Collapsing one section of ceiling or stretch of wall could end up causing other sections to break. Support beams break, more weight gets put onto other areas of the structure, etc. Magick does not exist in a vacuum; a Storyteller could maintain that causing mass destruction will come back to the Mage, even if Paradox isn't involved.<br /> <br /> This is why I don't care for the word &quot;Overpowered&quot; to be used so liberally. It doesn't always take into account the larger context of the game world the play is set in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-16-2017, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:05:56-08:00","id":1050046,"title":"","content":"<b>Cazador, Rad-Scorpions, Octopodes (Life 2).</b><br /> <br /> Those little babies I made for an Etherite of mine. I was looking at Life 2, thinking how to make better use of that. So, I came up to those... And I realized that I could create a deadly supernatural army using Life 2 alone. And, that mages are pretty fucked up beings.<br /> <br /> You can have infinity variations here - the CrabKings, giant crabs hunters, even insane gigantic amebae hunters... &quot;Ents&quot; (hunter trees), and one of my favorites, the &quot;Nydus Worms&quot;...<br /> <br /> Well, have you ever played Starcraft? So, think &quot;Zerg&quot; and go for the most vulgar grotesque monsters your sick mind can concoct<br /> <br /> Cazador are gaint bees, and Rad Scorpions giant Scorpions (dah)... If anyone ever played Fallout will know them.<br /> <br /> Octopodes are... My little personal touch. They are... Octopus... With several changes to allow for breathing and walking inland.<br /> <br /> Those obviously vulgar things can only be made on Vat tanks, s\u00f3 you'll need a serious lab for that. After growing your pets, pherormones are used to mark targets and non-targets (basically, an Life 1 connected on them). The octopodes inky is replaced with acid, and they are little devils when swarming an enemy at the hundreds.<br /> <br /> After I created the Octopodes, a friend of mine, who also loves the Etherite and loved the idea of those little creeps, so, the Octopobazooka was born.<br /> <br /> <b>Octopobazooka</b> - Octopus are fascinating creatures; even more fascinating is that their simple structures are easy to manipulate. With an well equiped lab and some Vat Tanks, they can be grown in just a few hours. Mechanical medical braces are a must have within the Vats, because many of the procedures need cirurgical intervention, but you can programe several braces to operate simultaneously, so you can safely breed some dozens every hour or so.<br /> <br /> First, you need to connect their stomachs with several key arteries of the heart; the stomach will be their new &quot;lungs&quot;. Some modifications in the muscles will provide the necessary ventilation (you'll find the exact incision points on the appendix manual; if you're familiar with programming in java, the arquive contains the files to make those automatic by the medical robotic braces of the Vat Tank, youll need only to supervise). Next, an infusion of hormones and nutrients in the tank will induce the necessary muscular changes to allow them to walk in land (and they do walk REALLY fast). An injection in their months of chemicals derived from turtles DNA will induce the local production of Cheratine, strenghtening their bites to make them capable of chewing steel. Also, this will produce several claws along their tentacles, allow them to cut flesh like butter (always try to throw them at your enemies faces, for maximum damage)<br /> <br /> Next, it comes the inky sack.While changing the stomachs, an sterilization of the acid producing cells is needed, and that first lay of stomachal skin must be carefully removed and transplanted into the inky sac. After that, they'll drop acid on enemies. It can use the claws of his tentacles, the strong bite and the acid to attack.<br /> <br /> This little monster than is made to segregate an chitinous membrane, that makes the creature to be enveloped in a big egg, were it will be storaged for later use.<br /> <br /> The Octopobazooka is a simple, and the better of all, total mundane device. Mount it on the back od a truck for use. This equipment is simply a kind of catapult (a cannon, actually) to launch the Octopodes. It has a cadence of 10 shoots/round, and a typical storage capacity of 100 eggs when mounted on the back of a pickup car (there are versions of that equip that uses Corr 4 to increase capacity, allowing 10 thousands eggs or even more, and uses of Forces 2 or even Time 3 to increase the fire rate... Think on a thing shooting thousands of little gremlin-like little monsters per round)<br /> <br /> Upon the impact, the egg breaks, and the Octopus inside will Hunt for its enemies.<br /> <br /> Those creatures have a short live span, and turn into a pool of acid upon death, which makes them even more dangerous, since they can commit full kamikaze attacks in order to destroy their targets.<br /> <br /> Those things make for excellent chantry guardians... But you better not suffer a backlash while manufacturing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:36:15-08:00","id":1050072,"title":"","content":"<b>Etherial Tracking Device (Prime 1)</b><br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> <b>Vital Etherial Marker (Prime 2)</b><br /> <br /> <br /> That's another piece of Engineering that I designed for Etherite use (I love the SoE).<br /> <br /> 1) Take a little chip, transistor, radio emmiter, whatever. As long as it is as small as possible, it's good. This small device will be henceforth called the &quot;trasmitter&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Now, you'll use another device, that will be henceforth called &quot;receiver&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3) Using Prime 1, you'll attune the etherial emanations of both devices towards one another, until their ressonance reaches a level of perfect atunement. It is recomended to turn this change into a permanent one.<br /> <br /> From now one, both devices will work as a single one.<br /> <br /> You can now use the transmitter to track any target. Place the pill sized device on his pocket, or use mundane means to attach it to his clothes, shoes, whatever (or use other effects - place the transmitter on a weapon with glue on it, and shoot on your target, that could be made with a mundane tech, or using Forces/Matter/Entropy/Corr effects).<br /> <br /> With the transmitter in the target, you can use any Correspondence effects on the target as if you had a live sample of him - no need to spend ANY success on Corr.<br /> <br /> You can use Corr 1 to always know where the transmitter is, with Corr 2 you can see everything around the target effortlessly, and you can cast any effect on him as if he were within your line of sight.<br /> <br /> The Prime 2 version is even more powerful, and there is the benefit that you don't risk your device being discovered and discarded by the target.<br /> <br /> With the Prime 2 version, you need to inject a nuclear isotope on the target - you can do that with a handshake or a pressure gun. The isotope is small enough to enter the skin of the target (it's subatomic), so you don't need a dart to pierce his skin (althouth you can). You can place it inside his drink, in a doornut, on the inside of his clothes, whatever.<br /> <br /> The important thing is: this isotope is prime-attuned to a receiver device. After succesfully implanting the isotope on the target (by whatever means), you can configure your receiver's etherial emanations to match those of the target.<br /> <br /> After that... Well, the target is your bitch. You can use effects on him from the other side of the globe as if he were in front of you. Not only that - since your receiver is as good as having the target's blood or DNA sample, you have some serious bonuses to affect him (I strongly suggest making the Prime 2 version a permanent pattern change of your receiver device. You'll turn your target EXTREMELY vulnerable to ANY of your magiks)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T15:48:35-08:00","id":1050122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1049936#post1049936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Ton of Bricks rote is really overpowered as it can potentially do a lot more damage than a direct effect rote unless you require a large number of successes. It also handwaves away a bunch of stuff like buildings actually being really difficult to demolish.<br /> <br /> There's a very similar example on p440 of the M20 rules where an <b>Enlightenment 7</b> character knocks down a pillar with a similar strength as a brick wall, but that example has six successes going for it. A rote like this that needs to do major damage to a building should need a minimum of 4 or more successes to work (4 successes +1 for forces = 10 health levels vs durability 4 structure 6 brick walls)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are far worse things you can do. Like say, transform concrete into gas. You now have a room temperature gaseous concrete that is about to horribly murder everything as thermodynamic laws start working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T15:57:28-08:00","id":1050124,"title":"","content":"If you are using &quot;Like a Ton of Bricks&quot; you have clearly bean backed in to Maxim 20 (If you're not willing to shell your own position, you're not willing to win.) territory, either that or you are a firm believer in Maxim's 6 (If violence wasn\u2019t your last resort, you failed to resort to enough of it.) 27 (Don't be afraid to be the first to resort to violence.) 37 (There is no 'overkill.' There is only 'open fire' and 'I need to reload.) and a few others. and no storyteller should feel that any setpice is safe around you.<br /> <br /> If you are going to start using &quot;Like a Ton of Bricks&quot; you should start asking questions about your environment. Don't attack the structure as a whole but the mortar holding the bricks in that section of wall in place, the pins &amp; seals holding the window pane in place, also be prepared to Scarper, because if they survive that attack you shouldn't have bean tangling with them in the first place. even if you just bring down some Dress Facade or a floating ceiling it's a distraction giving you enough time to Leg It.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:10:58-08:00","id":1050641,"title":"","content":"It's the number of successes required to get Ton of Bricks working that I'm concerned with. As written it's implied that you can knock down a wall with one success whereas I'm saying that you'd need at least four to even punch a hole in one. Yes it's highly situational but in that case it should be mentioned in the Rote's 'system/how it works' section. Effects that let you do potentially substantially more damage than the 'Base Damage or Duration Chart' need to be carefully vetted.<br /> <br /> Poorly thought out effects are a potentially big problem with Mage (although it does depend on playstyle), especially when they are disseminated as 'play tested'.<br /> <br /> Here are three Entropy/time effects for a mage who likes to shoot things. These are not tested.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Head Shot (Entropy 3, optionally with Prime 2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The mage makes a lucky head shot doing substantial damage.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">System: Enlightenment roll, base two successes to negate the increased difficulty of a head shot, additional successes add extra dice of damage, spend one Quintessence for aggravated damage.<br /> (Notes: Simple Entropy effect is used to negate the difficulties of a head shot)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Gangsta-Style (Entropy 3, Time 3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Negates the penalties for using two pistols at once and also makes those guns fire a lot faster.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">System: Roll Enlightenment, two successes is one extra action per turn, three successes is two extra actions per turn, lasts for one scene. No penalties for firing two weapons at once - both weapons use the combatants full Dexterity + Firearms dice pool.<br /> (Notes: Entropy negates difficulties of firing two weapons while Time allows those weapons to be fired faster)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Missed Me! (Entropy 3, Time 3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">By skipping backwards in time a moment the Mage changes their movements so that the attack that just hit them misses instead.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">System: Roll immediately after being hit (provided it was not an incapacitating attack) at +3 difficulty, each success negates one attack. Cannot be used if any other Time based Effect is ongoing. If the spell fails lose the next turn.<br /> (Notes: This rote is a multi turn time effect rolled up into a single effect. The expanded actions work like this: turn 1 - mage is hit by attack, turn 2 - Mage turns back time, turn 1 (again) - Mage changes action to dodge attack with Entropy effect)</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 02-17-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:52:29-08:00","id":1050698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050641#post1050641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the number of successes required to get Ton of Bricks working that I'm concerned with. As written it's implied that you can knock down a wall with one success whereas I'm saying that you'd need at least four to even punch a hole in one. Yes it's highly situational but in that case it should be mentioned in the Rote's 'system/how it works' section. Effects that let you do potentially substantially more damage than the 'Base Damage or Duration Chart' need to be carefully vetted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it must be vetoed. If I use Corr 4, Matter 2, Prime 2 to summon an Anvil in the ionosphere to go full Looney Toones on my foe, how much damage would I cause with a free fall anvil? (Not to mention that it will probably be on fire). And, how much damage will I cause using Corr 4 to teleport the target 200 km (100 miles) up? And how much damage will I cause the target, if I use Corr 5 to make him co-locate himself with Earth, thus falling in free fall until the center of the planet, and being cooked alive by the intense temperatures? And how much damage if I open a portal to the Sun in the face of an enemy?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050641#post1050641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Head Shot (Entropy 3, optionally with Prime 2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The mage makes a lucky head shot doing substantial damage.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">System: Enlightenment roll, base two successes to negate the increased difficulty of a head shot, additional successes add extra dice of damage, spend one Quintessence for aggravated damage.<br /> (Notes: Simple Entropy effect is used to negate the difficulties of a head shot)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Why Entropy 3 instead of 2?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050641#post1050641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Gangsta-Style (Entropy 3, Time 3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Negates the penalties for using two pistols at once and also makes those guns fire a lot faster.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">System: Roll Enlightenment, two successes is one extra action per turn, three successes is two extra actions per turn, lasts for one scene. No penalties for firing two weapons at once - both weapons use the combatants full Dexterity + Firearms dice pool.<br /> (Notes: Entropy negates difficulties of firing two weapons while Time allows those weapons to be fired faster)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, why Entropy 3 instead of 2?<br /> <br /> And here, a few notes - the penalties for using 2 weapons is -2 to your right hand and -4 to the offhand. Entropy allows you to get extra dice, like in &quot;magik enhancing skills&quot;. So, in order to nullify those penalties, you'd need 6 successes... Am I right? Plus any success you'd like for extra shootings with Time.<br /> <br /> A better alternative is to simply use Mind 1 and emulate the merit &quot;ambidextrous&quot;, thus removing all penalties with a single success, and adding the Time effect on top of that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050641#post1050641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#2e75b5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Missed Me! (Entropy 3, Time 3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">By skipping backwards in time a moment the Mage changes their movements so that the attack that just hit them misses instead.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">System: Roll immediately after being hit (provided it was not an incapacitating attack) at +3 difficulty, each success negates one attack. Cannot be used if any other Time based Effect is ongoing. If the spell fails lose the next turn.<br /> (Notes: This rote is a multi turn time effect rolled up into a single effect. The expanded actions work like this: turn 1 - mage is hit by attack, turn 2 - Mage turns back time, turn 1 (again) - Mage changes action to dodge attack with Entropy effect)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Time 4. Entropy is not necessary (the Mage will have the chance to roll again. You can use Entropy 2 if you wanna extra dice for your dodge or to remove dices from your opponent's attack, but that's some extra effect, it's not necessary for such a &quot;second chance&quot; effect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-17-2017, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T14:29:54-08:00","id":1050720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1049784#post1049784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power Sink<br /> (Mind 2, Prime 2)<br /> Sometimes it is enough to appear powerful...<br /> To this end this rote gives some unidentifiable power to your aura for others to notice.<br /> <br /> Related is the \u201cfailure\u201c to hide the power you posess. A short slip in the veil you constructed to hide your terrifying might.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think you'd need Mind 2 AND Prime 2 for that. Rather, you can do that effect with Mind 2 OR Prime 2.<br /> <br /> With Prime 2, you can do a Vulgar effect that will amplify your ressonance to palatable levels. In terms of mechanics, how about this - each success gives a temporary increase of 1 point on one of your ressonances (or 1 point in 2 ressonance, or 1 point in each one of the 3, as you see fit). With 5 points in anyone ressonance, reality warps around you, and your power aura is the kind of shit to turn your pants brown (5 Jhor will make ghosts visible for example, plants will wither and die, things will become rusty, your very breath may be a frozen air, etc. A dinamic 5 will cause electrical storms around you, and pattern 5 will stop even the air, even raindrops will halt on air, living creatures, everything will halt, and so on).<br /> <br /> With Mind 2, it's just a majestic aura, a mix of awe and terror to anyone that looks at you. In little doses it's coincidental, making people hold you on high regards, as someone to be respected and feared. But, if people start bending down on their knees at the very sight of you, filled with aspirations and terror for looking at a &quot;living God&quot; (if, for example, you put 20+ successes on it), it will be vulgar as hell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T14:38:01-08:00","id":1050725,"title":"","content":"Now, you guys were talking about overpowered? Well... I'll give you overpowered.<br /> <br /> That's a brutal one. And a personal little pet of mine.<br /> <br /> <b>Damn to Hell</b> (Correspondence 5) - The master of correspondence can make several things occupy a same space at the same time.<br /> <br /> With this effect, thats what the m\u00e1ster will do with his target... And everything else.<br /> <br /> Basically, the target will &quot;share&quot; the same space... As everything else.<br /> <br /> Meaning: he will sink inside the planets core... In free fall.<br /> <br /> The huge temperatures of the planets core will take care of vaporizing the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T14:49:11-08:00","id":1050731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050725#post1050725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you guys were talking about overpowered? Well... I'll give you overpowered.<br /> <br /> That's a brutal one. And a personal little pet of mine.<br /> <br /> <b>Damn to Hell</b> (Correspondence 5) - The master of correspondence can make several things occupy a same space at the same time.<br /> <br /> With this effect, thats what the m\u00e1ster will do with his target... And everything else.<br /> <br /> Basically, the target will &quot;share&quot; the same space... As everything else.<br /> <br /> Meaning: he will sink inside the planets core... In free fall.<br /> <br /> The huge temperatures of the planets core will take care of vaporizing the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you already share the space of everything, why bother with falling? The Victim IS already in the same space as the core of the Earth.<br /> <br /> Also I don't consider a Master level effect to kill someone &quot;cheating&quot;<br /> <br /> Some STs would rate this as a godlike feat, thus requiring more successes (20?) as simply dealing damage (4 for 8 levels)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T15:15:22-08:00","id":1050752,"title":"","content":"Now, that next one may have profound impacts on the scenario.<br /> <br /> <b>Memory Storage USB</b> (Mind 3, Prime 2)<br /> <br /> This effect allows the Mage to storage <i>memories</i> on objects for later use.<br /> <br /> The best use of this effect however, is to storage <i>skills</i>.<br /> <br /> The VA are particularly good at this, and they can storage any skill them have on Pen Drivers, which they can share amonsgt each other.<br /> <br /> Worth of notice, this effect can also be used to <i>copy</i> the storaged memories between different objects.<br /> <br /> Any one that possess an USB-skill can use another effect, <b>Memory Integrational Retrieve</b> (Mind 3) to access the memories contained in the storage device, and gain access to whatever skills it may contain.<br /> <br /> Each successes in the effect <i>Memory storage USB</i> places one memory inside the recipient or one skill point that the caster possess; and each success on the effect <i>Memory Integrational Retrieve</i> allows access to one memory or to one skill contained within (up to the maximum skill level contained).<br /> <br /> It is said that the VA keep a huge virtual library not of books or enconded knowledge that you need to study in order to absorb the information, but rather, it's a library of <i>pure thoughts</i>, of direct <i>mental knowledge</i>, which you can turn on and off, like a switch, without needing the hard effort of learning it.<br /> <br /> It's said that the VA have many useful skills storaged, which they past and copy among each other, on regular basis. The VA masters puts a huge value on new skills they dont have in their library yet; such prices are higly valued, because once a new skill is added on their secret mental library, it is forever after avaiable towards ALL members of the Tradition that knows how to access it. <br /> <br /> Those VAs with the necessary Prestige background, can access the library without ANY effect whatsoever; the masters of the VA keep an effect on the library that allows the apprentices within the Tradition to download the memories using only their computers. All that the VA will need afterwards will be Mind 3 to gain access to the skill.<br /> <br /> You can consider that the VA mental library have ANY possible skill at lvl 5 AT LEAST (I'll explain that one).<br /> <br /> The VA Masters have developed a very powerful effect to keep their library up to date<br /> <br /> <b>Quantum Skill</b> (Entropy 5)<br /> <br /> Each success gives the Mage one dot on ANY skill. Even if this makes him go beyond 5.<br /> <br /> The VA reach this using super quantum computers, capable of generating tought processes that would be impossible by any other means.<br /> <br /> So, with that, the Masters can use the Mind 3 Prime 2 rote to keep the copies of their skills up to level 10.<br /> <br /> So, there is a high likelyhood that the VA can download skills up to level 10 from their shared library.<br /> <br /> Just remember the rules for pattern leaking and permadox for skills beyond 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T02:31:40-08:00","id":1050921,"title":"","content":"&gt;why Entropy 3 instead of 2<br /> For the Headshot rote you're right, it should be 2, however for the two gun rote I'm requiring a higher level of entropy as it is more like controlling then influencing. Entropy has some pretty subtle distinctions between 2 and 3 and I'm choosing that this effect is more difficult to pull off than a similar but easier Mind 1/Entropy 2 effect.<br /> <br /> With regards to Time in the M20 sphere descriptions you can 'Rewind Time' and retcon an action at rank 3, not 4 which is what inspired me to work up this particular rote and I'm trying to emulate the OP with clever uses of spheres rather than going straight to full on Archmage levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 02-18-2017, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T07:23:18-08:00","id":1050988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050921#post1050921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;why Entropy 3 instead of 2<br /> For the Headshot rote you're right, it should be 2, however for the two gun rote I'm requiring a higher level of entropy as it is more like controlling then influencing. Entropy has some pretty subtle distinctions between 2 and 3 and I'm choosing that this effect is more difficult to pull off than a similar but easier Mind 1/Entropy 2 effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy 3 is control over matter. Entropy 2 is control of probabilities, control of odds. It doesn't matter if an effect is easier/harder to do, that is represented by a higher amount of successes needed, no by requiring bigger Sphere levels.<br /> <br /> For example, look at the rote &quot;octopodes&quot; that I put just a little above. Turning a squid into a freaking killing machine is by no means easy... But it still requires only Life 2... <b>Because that's what Life 2 does</b> (change simple life - invertebrates and bellow).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1050921#post1050921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Time in the M20 sphere descriptions you can 'Rewind Time' and retcon an action at rank 3, not 4 which is what inspired me to work up this particular rote and I'm trying to emulate the OP with clever uses of spheres rather than going straight to full on Archmage levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 3 in M20? Because in Revised it was Time 4 if I'm not mistaken... Well, I think this is too overpowered for a level 3 power, but if M20 made that way, well... I prefer to keep it Time 4 nevertheless, for balance sake","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T11:05:45-08:00","id":1051069,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> I think the differences in our approaches are down to the differences between revised and 20th anniversary. I've never played revised so I'm reading from the M20 book which seems to have subtle balance changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:38:14-08:00","id":1051187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1051069#post1051069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I think the differences in our approaches are down to the differences between revised and 20th anniversary. I've never played revised so I'm reading from the M20 book which seems to have subtle balance changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just checked, probability control is still Entropy 2. Entropy 3 is still control of matter patterns (basically, to break or to fix something). So, those effects are still Entropy 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T16:39:15-08:00","id":1051212,"title":"","content":"Well, possibilities are limitless, actually. As an effort of creativity, I always try to come with the best uses from levels 1-3 of Spheres, specially levels 1 and 2, for maximum impact over all those green Mages out there. So, lets try a little list<br /> <br /> <b>Correspondence 1</b><br /> <br /> <u>Sonar Vision</u> - Remember the Batman movie, the Dark Knight? His sonar vision, that allowed him to see foes over the walls and in total darkness? Yep, that's not an insignificant thing.<br /> Also, use Correspondence 1, Forces 1, and you can have that machine that he built that can track anyone by the voice, which he used to track the Joker (in the case of the device, it would be a wonder built using Prime, but anyway).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forces 1</b> - Forces 1 need some talk about, because the amount of things it can do is impressive. So, here are some of the top of my mind, but certanly not the only ones<br /> <br /> <u>Heat Vision/X Ray Vision</u> - very useful to see in the dark; alternatively, <u>Dark Sight</u> for more mystical paradigms, that allows you to see at total dark as if it were totally bright day (with color vision).<br /> <br /> <u>Seismic Sense</u> - that is the same sense that many animals (some reptiles, insects, arachnide and several others) have to perceive tiny vibrations on the soil. This sense can even be used to perceive Vampires using Obfuscate or other creatures with similar supernatural means of concealing. With this sense, you can locate precisely where the source of the vibrations come, as well as many other informations - size, weight. <br /> What's more, you can have this toghether with <u>Sonar Sense</u>, allowing you to sense any sound vibrations, like an owl or a bat.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces 2</b> - that's also another level VERY useful (and I say this as someone who doesn't like the Forces Sphere at all). A few examples of this versatility, beyond the classicals telekinetic, pirocinesis/cryocinesys<br /> <br /> <u>Invisibility</u> - just like that. Unlike a power like Obfuscation, this is not just a mental trick, it's true light invisibility.<br /> Toghether with <u>Muffled Sounds</u> (that works like level 1 Quietus, removing all sound), it means that you can walk around COMPLETELY indetectable by regular senses (you can still be detected by several supernatural means)<br /> True, absolute invisibility (meaning: being totally indetectable by ANY means - unless the one trying to find you can surpass your successes in your supernatural invisibility) would require... Hum... Let me think... Mind 1 to hide all your psichic emanations... Prime 2 to hide all your ressonance... And maybe Life 3+ to make your vitals undetectable? Maybe you'll also need Correspondence 2 IF you wanna be absolutely sure that not even Correspondence senses can pick you up, and Entropy 2 to &quot;disguise&quot; your &quot;destiny role&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, there you have it, <u>True Invisibility</u> - Forces 2, Mind 1, Prime 2, Life 3, Entropy 2<br /> That's a lot of spheres but... This effect don't need to be applied as a single one, because in fact, each of those spheres can be cast as a different effect. That means that, a group of 4-6 initial PCs could do it without trouble.<br /> <br /> <u>Concussive Grenade</u> - you don't even need this as an effect, because you can ACTUALLY purchase this kind of mundane grenades. But, since military grade equipment may not always be a viable option, you can do this. A strong blinding light, with a strong, deafning sound. The purpose of this is to disorient the enemy. Enemies with heightned senses on will suffer.<br /> <br /> <u>Simple Ilusions</u> - the famous &quot;hologram-like&quot; illusions. Those are not mental tricks, but rather visual and sound illusions. Therefore, mind shields and other kinds of mental defenses won't show it's true nature (which could make it more believable). Hell, you can even have this effect with a kind of kinect force, making &quot;solid light&quot;, so, an illusory brick wall made of light would be as &quot;solid&quot; as a real one (that will work as a force field, toghether along the light manipulation). Complex illusions (like illusions that can react to the viewer, like an illusory cat that can talk with the person), will need constant concentration of the Mage, unless he adds Entropy 2 for some simple interactions (like a robot that allows anyone who says a password to pass) or Mind 3, Entropy 2 for really complex things (like engaging in conversation).<br /> And, if you wanna go really hardcore on the level of weird and ridiculously vulgar that you can get, make your illusion permanent (with lots of successes), and use Spirit 3 to awaken it's spirit (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <u>Wind Message</u> (Forces 2, Corr 2) - that's not so useful or so powerful, but it's a classic. When you enter the evil necrimancer's Tower, the lich's cave... And you hear his evil laughs echoing all around? Yep, that's it...<br /> Talk hear, and be heard over there. Simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-18-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:05:07-08:00","id":1051224,"title":"","content":"<b>Life 2</b> - <u>Plants</u><br /> <br /> most people see Life 2 only as a source of self healing. That Sphere level, however, probably is one of the most insanely powerful levels that are.<br /> <br /> With Life 2, you can control plants to a huge degree, in that manner of fantasy descriptions of druids that make the florest hunt his enemies. While in the woods, you can make plants entangle enemies, binding them, suffocating, and attacking.<br /> <br /> You can also make plants cover your body, giving you a kind of &quot;wood armor&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's just the beggining; after that, you can make all the <i>modifications</i><br /> <br /> It would be really hard to list all the modifications you can make to plants, but there are almost infinity possibilities; plant guardians for your chantry can be very Powerful (does anybody here remember that crazy Oak from Harry Potter that would smash anyone that get close with it's colossal strenght?). A Chantry protected by plants permanently modified with Life 2 will be a hellish place to try to invade (actually, the chantry itself can be made into a living organism that can fight to defend itself). And, a simple Life 1 effect (Pherormones!) can be used to control the chantry's pets, allowing them to tell friends from foes.<br /> <br /> Other modifications to plants include:<br /> <br /> Special drugs and substances production - did you know that Kevlar is an organic substance? You could have plants that produce chitin (the same substance of nails, insects exosqueletons and ivory, a very tough substance that could be used even for making armors), spider silk as strong as steel (more actually), alcahool (very useful is a fuel and power source), several kinds of acids, poisons, drugs. And they could produce those on massive amounts. All those plants could be modified in a matter of days, maybe even hours or minutes (well, since you'll be doing all this in your chantry, you won't need to worry about the paradox).<br /> <br /> With just Matter 2, you can have your precious plants to produce gasoline, oil, kevlar, plastics of all sorts. You can have an industrialized raw matterial production fully grow... Just &quot;cultivate&quot; your &quot;oil refinery&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's only with plants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-18-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:37:08-08:00","id":1051239,"title":"","content":"<b>Life 2</b> - <u>Microbes</u><br /> <br /> Well...<br /> <br /> What's really the limit here? First of all, just build your very own custom-designed disease. Contagion agent (air, water, blood, skin contact, animal transmissor - insects, birds, livestook, consuption of contaminated food, etc). Determine the symptons (hemorragic, behavioral changes, alergic reactions, necrosis of tissue, diarrhea, fever, convulsions, heart attack, coma, death - whatever). Has anyone saw movies like &quot;I'm the Legend&quot; or &quot;Z War&quot; (I guess it was that, with Brad Pitt)? About insanely angry zombies? Well, there is a disease of the real world (in portuguese it is called &quot;Rage&quot;, I don't know in english) that changes the behavior of the affected (it's the mad dogs disease, that makes dogs extremely violent, trasmitted by their saliva). So... You could turn people (or dogs) into mindless drones of pure rage (again, life 1 - Pherormones! - can keep those zombies from attacking you). S\u00edfilis is another behavioral changer disease. It makes people affected to be... Always horny. A pitty that both of those diseases will cause a horrible death to those affected, because I would love to be affected by a &quot;lust disease&quot; without further side effects.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can use Life 2 to make yogurts, bread, cheese, ale, wine.<br /> <br /> You can use Life 2 to become the enviromental cleaner too. Use it to purify an area of any &quot;wyrm taint&quot;. You can do this by creating pollution-eater microbes, that can eat plastic and, since you're a Mage, maybe even plumb and arsenic.<br /> <br /> You could also produce microbes that can do things that would need bigger Life levels, in theory, but thats up to the ST. You could in theory, produce a v\u00edrus that increase your brain capacity (giving more mental attributes), or bacteria that can increase your physical attributes, or that can \u00edndice specific changes. Too overpowered? Maybe, maybe not. First of all, it's not direct control. So, the ST can state that any such changes take days, or weeks, or months, or even years, to happen (so, no super mutant v\u00edrus that gives you super strenght or steel skin in a few seconds only). The attributes increase may be capped to only 1 by this method, and without the capacity of going above 5. The change may linger for a few days... And disappear forever afterwards (your imunologic system made you &quot;immune&quot; to those blessings... Build a new virus pal - or use Life 3 to change your imune system, but at this point, its easier to simply use Life 3 to those effects). And... It's possible to have some side effects (but I would leave those for paradox).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-18-2017, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:02:06-08:00","id":1051251,"title":"","content":"<b>Life 2</b> - <u>Animals</u><br /> <br /> Life 2 can change any invertabrates. That can be used to make VERY powerful swarms of Guardian pets. I've already gave the examples of the Octopodes, Cazador and Rad Scorpions. But really, possibilities are outstanding. Giant spiders, giant squids, colossal worms moving inside the Earth, giant cnidarians (they are called &quot;living waters&quot; in portuguese, I don't know in english). Those guardians (and hunters) can be built with massive strenght, great speed, natural weaponry (fangs, claws, body needles like porcupines, and even ranged needles attacks, muscle propeled). They can also have many kinds of venons, acids, can bind enemies with paralisers, spider silk, they can spit venon or even acid, and can even have electrical attacks... Or... Have any one here saw the Startroopers movie? Where they have the giant insect that spits fire? Yep, a giant insect that amass hidrogen, or a very strong acid, could spit fire... And all that would be only Life 2.<br /> <br /> So, basically, with Life 2 a Mage can make an army of Zergs from StarCraft, or the army of Insects from Startroops.<br /> <br /> Just imagine the most powerful Progenitor's Constructs as the most nightmarish jungle-hells imaginable...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:24:50-08:00","id":1051266,"title":"","content":"<b>Bard Tongue</b> - Mind 3, Entropy 2<br /> <br /> That curse is... Well... You won't like it on you.<br /> <br /> Whatever the target thinks it will be the worse thing it could happen... It will.<br /> <br /> This effect had a colossal failure during the Himalain war, were a Eutanathoi cursed an enemy Akashic with this effect, but the wise monk used his Mind control to self induce him to think that the worse thing it could happen to him would be to kill the Euthanatos that cursed him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:26:30-08:00","id":1051354,"title":"","content":"<b>Entropy 1</b><br /> <br /> <u>Danger Sense</u> - as per the name. Makes a lot harder to make traps on you, and acidents much more unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:12:01-08:00","id":1051607,"title":"","content":"<b>Predict Enemy</b> - Time 2, Entropy 1<br /> <br /> Each success in this effect reduces by -1 the difficult for attacking, dodging or any other combat roll (min 3), for as long as the duration. Further more, you'll get a subconscious awareness of what your foe plans to do next (basically, the ST will tell you your enemies actions in advance, and you'll be able to act according to it)<br /> <br /> <b>Ultra Precision</b> - Entropy 2<br /> Each success in this gives an automatic success on a skill test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-19-2017, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:25:33-08:00","id":1051613,"title":"","content":"<b>Minor Curse</b> - Entropy 2<br /> <br /> Each success in this effect cancels one success of an skill roll of your target. If you get more successes in this effect than the target's, it will botch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:36:16-08:00","id":1051615,"title":"","content":"<b>Luck Aura</b> - Entropy 2<br /> <br /> Whenever a good thing happens, it seeks you out first. And bad things will dodge from you.<br /> <br /> Each success grants you one random positive event, or divert one random negative event. For example, if in a scene, someone would find a $100 note in the floor, that would be you. If someone would be hit by a car - that WOULDN'T be you.<br /> This effect makes more sense as an ritual with at least 1 day duration, and it's a great way to ensure survivability (at the ST discretion) by giving you an edge were you'll always seem to be on the right spot at the right time.<br /> It is recomended that the ST do the rolls in secret, and that the ST also keep the &quot;good luck&quot; account in secret from the player. On many occasions, a fortuitous happenstance may have just occured without the ST even being notified (like a guard that took a turn it otherwise wouldn't, at the exactly same moment the PC was sneeking inside the compound), so the player will never really know how much &quot;good fortune&quot; he still have left.<br /> That's a very powerful effect, althouth those that come to rely on luck too much may become too overconfident, and end up oon trouble when their luck runs out.<br /> <br /> (Of course, the player can use Entropy 1 to have a vague impression of how much &quot;good luck&quot; he still have left)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-19-2017, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:59:21-08:00","id":1051655,"title":"","content":"<b>Eureka!</b> - Entropy 1<br /> Each success in this effect reduces the dif for any mental roll by -1 (min 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Mentalism</b> - Entropy 1 or Mind 1<br /> Each success in this effect reduces the dif for any social roll by -1 (min 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Fate Signals</b> - Entropy 1<br /> This effect allows the Mage to sense the thrends of Fate directly. He can sense any Entropy use or others powers that manipulate fate or chance, can sense the Destiny of someone (meaning, can sense the Destiny background or things like the flaw &quot;Dark Destiny&quot;), and can feel curses or blessings around (he can tell if someone ia using a power to give good fortune or bad luck for example, and so on)<br /> (On mechanics, basically tells the Mage of anything that could be made using any level of Entropy. The ST determines the amount of information that is achieved according to the successes - however, the stronger the effect, the easier to detect, meaning that a Mage with a 20 successes luck-aura would be lighthouse of Fate disturbance to the Mage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-19-2017, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:23:41-08:00","id":1051670,"title":"","content":"<b>Improving the Machine</b> - Entropy 3<br /> This effect can have VERY powerful consequences. It is used to improve the capacity and the quality of ANY equipment, or to manufacture, using apropriate skills, some equip. So, here's a small (but not complete) list of what it can do, and the equipments may have SEVERAL of those improvements at once; when building a machine or piece of equip, all those modifications are permanent, otherwise, used on already made things they just give temporary boosts<br /> - Give an additional +1 damage to any kind of weapons (be it a sword, fireweapons or a club), above any bonuses it may already have<br /> - Give +1 soak for armor<br /> - Remove any flaws from the equipment, even if they aren't visible;<br /> - Make a broken machine work<br /> - Make it easier to use, reducing dif by -1;<br /> - Making it possible to built the item in a smaller/bigger or lightier/heavier version, as wished (only when used to build an item)<br /> - Increasing the speed/efficiency of a machine (faster computers, with programs with fewer bugs, firearms with a better rate of fire, gatlin machibeguns less prone to overheat, vaccum cleaners with more sucking power, cars with more acceleration, increased potency, more fuel efficient, less polluent, etc)<br /> - Increased durability<br /> - &quot;Self-correction System&quot;, giving 1 extra success in any skill use of the equipment (self balanced swords and knives, guns with correctional damping, cars with balance self adjustment, computers with inteligent directional self corrector software - whatever it is, that one will need a good description from the player).<br /> No matter what changes, this effect only make POSSIBLE changes (meaning, improvements that would be conveivable with high levels of skills for manufacture - even if it would be epic beyond 6+ levels). For <i>impossible</i> changes (like making a battery out of milk or making your wooden sword as strong as steel and as sharp as a lightsaber, or making your computer be able to hack people's minds) you'll need other spheres (mostly, Matter)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-19-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:17:52-08:00","id":1051708,"title":"","content":"<b>Detect Supernatural</b> - Spirit 1, Prime 1<br /> You can dectect supernatural beings around, and with some knowledge of specific lore, you can tell which kind they are (Vampire, Werewolf, Changelling, Mage, Fomori, Drone, Mummy, Demon, Spirit, Wraith, whatever).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:51:17-08:00","id":1051721,"title":"","content":"<b>Spirit 2</b> - Summon Spirit<br /> <br /> Now, that's a special case power. This, right here, is basically the power of Shamans. Almost everything Shamans will do will be <b>right here</b>.<br /> <br /> This is a VERY peculiar power, because it is absolutely <i>inderect</i>, and requires a LOT of things beyond a simple Paradigm/focus and Arete roll.<br /> <br /> You'll summon a spirit, and you'll have to bargain with him for his help. Those bargains may be very complex or very simple things; if you're a lazy ST like me hehe, you'll just ask for some quintessence tax and be done with it. However, asking favors are a VERY interesting way to deal with this, specially since you can get the smart-boy Shaman who thinks he can do everything with one single spell, but end up against the wall. The best way to use this is: spirits have allies and enemies too. So, if you bargain with spirits A, B and C, you'll gain the enmity of X, Y, Z. That's the price you pay for that power. So, you'll have to choose. Give the player a big list of possibilities - but, some things he would want... Well, sadly, he choose the wrong side. <br /> <br /> Also, spirits are assholes. Have the Shaman NEED a series of self-imposed flaws in exchange for all those wonderful paradox-free powers. So, never using anything artificially made, means that the Mage will basically be treated as a homeless person in any &quot;civilized&quot; community (cities and the like). It must be things that will have a serious impact, and the bigger the impact, the more power it potentially wields. Another option: follow the footsteps of Odin, and pluck one of your eyes away to &quot;gain wisdom&quot; (yuck!).<br /> <br /> Sacrifices little children! That's a good one... A good one that the Union don't understand... But thats why the Traditions fight for right? To preserve their freedom and way of life... Including the possibility of human sacrifices for the spirits to give you power.<br /> <br /> So... How about trying to give it a few mechanics?<br /> <br /> The way I do it: the powers spirits give are related to the level of &quot;commitment&quot; the Shaman has to pleasing them. So, I simply number the possible sacrifices from 1 to 5, and let the Mage ask for powers that could be mimic with spheres at maximum level of the level of his sacrifice. So, human sacrifice is a level 4 offering, while <i>children</i> sacrifice is the mighty level 5. So, a Shaman could sacrifice a child to ask for a Spirit to give him Primium (Matter 5), or the power to shapeshift into a real dragon (Life 5) or to go back in time (Time 5). Animal sacrifice won't work, unless the Mage raise the animal as a personal pet, in which case is a level 3 sacrifice. Offerings of quintessence are always level 2. Plucking your own eye is a permanent level 3 ofering, your hand or leg, or both eyes or your tongue is 4. Sacrificing your own children or loved one is a permanent level 5 sacrifice. (Meaning, you can gain one permanent &quot;spiritual power-favor&quot; free of paradox with the same effect as a power with maximum Sphere of 5. Are you THAT power hunger? Or THAT desperate? Or... Is your loved one AND you so aware of the dire situation you are, that you both know that this is THE ONLY WAY?).<br /> <br /> Services must be just as significant. What would that be, it's up to the ST, but hardly a service will be significant enough to earn an eternal permanent &quot;favor&quot; in the form of a charm from a spirit.<br /> <br /> A few ideas: <br /> -Cannibalism of the Dead (alone or in adition with sacrifices) - Level 4;<br /> -Consecration of the Dead (mummification technics*, proper burial, cremation, etc) - Level 3<br /> -Upholding the spirits ideals (Never refuse hospitality, never lie, never eat meat, poverty vote, chastidy, never refuse a challenge for a duel, never run from a fight, always trick your friends and enemies, never do an honest day of work and always steal what you need, and many others) Variable<br /> Fighting for the spirits Wars and enemies - Variable, according to the level of the enemy and commitment to the cause<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *not to confuse to the spell of Life from Mummy the Ressurection","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-19-2017, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T16:46:18-08:00","id":1051749,"title":"","content":"<b>Consecration</b> - Spirit 3, Prime 2<br /> Consecrate your clothes, weapons and equipments to change along with you, so, if you use Life to shapeshift yourself, they will adjust to your knew form, if you enter the Umbra they'll follow, and they even have astral's reflections if you leave your body, so you'll have your items even in your dreams or on astral projection.<br /> This effect will also make all your items share your ressonance. If the Mage do this to ALL his equipments and foci, all his rolls are made at -1 dif, both for mundane rolls and magical rolls (Arete rolls), and all his equip will malfunction with others (and may even try to activelly attack the user, thanks to the awaken spirit of the item), but people who get their hands on such items, can cast effects on him as if having his blood sample","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-19-2017, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T18:36:08-08:00","id":1051799,"title":"","content":"<b>Arcanum</b> - Entropy 2<br /> Each success in this effect temporarly increases the Mage's Arcanum rate by 1 (Max 10)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:51:08-08:00","id":1051877,"title":"","content":"Time 4--turn a candle into an explosive more powerful than a stick of dynamite. Probably most useful in earlier settings, but you can always carry candles with you in the modern age.<br /> <br /> Tallow and candle wax have several times more energy density than TNT. Unlike TNT, candles release that energy very slowly. But with Time 4, you can light a candle and cause it to release all its energy at once, by compressing its entire lifespan into an instant. Obviously Vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 02-20-2017, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T03:21:14-08:00","id":1051918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1051877#post1051877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 4--turn a candle into an explosive more powerful than a stick of dynamite. Probably most useful in earlier settings, but you can always carry candles with you in the modern age.<br /> <br /> Tallow and candle wax have several times more energy density than TNT. Unlike TNT, candles release that energy very slowly. But with Time 4, you can light a candle and cause it to release all its energy at once, by compressing its entire lifespan into an instant. Obviously Vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum... That is... Interesting... We can also... Well... <i>Compress</i> several explosions... Hum... Adding Corr 4, we could detonate several grenades, for example, freeze them on time just some microseconds after detonation, compress all those explosions on a tiny recipient (an empt pen, for example), and when needed... Just throw the pen at the enemy and KABOOM!!! 20 grenades exploding at the same time in a compressed way... Very powerful hum... Yeah, that's one way of doing &quot;magical&quot; items without the need of Prime... And, since you can prepare those in the safety of your Sanctum, you can avoid the terrible Paradox...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T03:54:51-08:00","id":1051929,"title":"","content":"I'll give some ideas of Spirit 2 summonings that may be useful, even if you're not a propor Shaman, and even if you're not willing to do bargain with the spiritual entities (or if you'll only go so far when bargaining)<br /> <br /> <b>Summon Banes</b> Spirit 2<br /> Banes are the entropic and evil spirits of the Wyrm, from the middle Umbra. Those beings can be a huge pain for the summoner if he isn't careful, but even so, they can be useful. They are very useful when you wanna to taint, desecrate or destroy an area; banes may even do it for &quot;free&quot; for you on some occasions. So, do you wanna kill a Verbena's sacred Tree? Do you wanna destroy the pure glade of some Dreamspeakers? A large group of Garou hiding in their Caern is causing you trouble? Well, those guys are here for you, and they'll charge you ALMOST nothing...<br /> Oh, do you have nature spirits angry at you? (Probably for such acts as I state above) Well, fear not, banes are friends!<br /> Just be careful when using those. Always weight the pros and cons before using banes... The ideal way to use them is the tactic of &quot;summon and hide&quot;. Summon them at the doorstep of those damn (insert enemy here), and run away.<br /> Beware of the Jhor that this effect causes thou.<br /> But, on the up side, with more Jhor, the easier it is to use this effect... And... The &quot;friendlier&quot; the banes become... Isn't that lovely?<br /> Now, if you're a Nephandi... To hell with the consequences! Just invite some thousands to live in your Sanctum, offer them some children and virgins sacrifices on regular bases, and have fun with a pletora of cool powers!<br /> For, it is best to rule on hell... And fuck up the Earth<br /> <br /> <b>Summon Pattern Spiders</b> - Spirit 2<br /> Now, Weaver spirits aren't always so helpful as banes, but you can also make use of them. Bargaining with Weaver spirits can be a little harder; they can demand that you stop disrupting reality, for example (never use Vulgar Magik, Level 5 sacrifice). That's their most common request in exchange for permanent help; however, they can give minor concessions IF the Mage agrees to keep high amounts of Pattern (the Mage ressonance must have at least 2 dots on Pattern above Entropy or Dinamism).<br /> Even without bargaining, those spiders can be summoned to <u>strenghten the Gauntlet</u>. They'll do their jobs automatically, as long as left alone. Clever Mages will summon pattern spiders in an area surrounding his chantry, to make harder the life of any spiritual invasor.<br /> Those spiders are also great if you're having problems with banes or wyldlings... Did you summon a bane to devour the totem of some dreamspeaker, and now the banes are bothering you? Never fear! The Weaver is here! Summon as many of those spiders as you can, and they'll calcify the banes...<br /> And you keep going attracting spiritual attention acting like this...<br /> But who cares right? Spirits are just tools after all, and we dont ask the Hammer how he feals about hitting the nail, am I right or am I right?<br /> <br /> <b>Summon Wyldlings</b> - Spirit 2<br /> Annnnnd, of course, those. Forget bargaining with those, unless you're a Marauder. Just summon and run (actually, summon, and EVERYBODY runs).<br /> Oh, and they'll do great against those pesk spiders trying to calcify you in the gauntlet for being a naughty boy.<br /> <br /> Keep summoning all the representations of the Triad to have them fight one another... That's a sure way to make friends. But, once again, who gives a damn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T04:22:32-08:00","id":1051933,"title":"","content":"<b>Summon Minor Demons</b> - Spirit 2<br /> No, that's not The Fallen. Those are beings from the High Umbra, spirits of mischief and mayhem. Not banes either.<br /> Demons are a diverse lot. Demonologist's manuals will describe countless types - Imps, Succubus, Incubbus, Rakshasas, Efrities, Yomi, Maeljins, Oni, and many, many others.<br /> Summoning demmons WONT make you an infernalist <i>right away</i>, but, it is EXTREMELY shun on the Traditions, and <i>forbatten</i> by the Union. Demonology is something that can quickly award you a court trial on the Traditions, and a trip to 101 for the Union. However, a Mage can keep this kind of business on... Respectable levels, as to not draw attention. Some demonologists can get the respect of their peers however, if they show that their Arts are used to study and to better fight those creatures, not to serve and bargain. But, to gain respect as a demonologist, is not hard.<br /> Demons are probably the kind of spirit more prone to bargaining. The most common and desired commodity is simple: the Mage's own soul. But, since not all Mages desire to sell their souls, demons are happy to bargain all sorts of &quot;inofensive&quot; things.<br /> The things demons ask may seem ilogical (specially for those not used to those creatures and that believe in the myths of hell and that they are absolutely evil, sadistic, etc). A succubus, for example, may ask the Mage to have sex with her... And that's one that A LOT of Mages do... Because... Well... The power she offers me... So much... For so little? Besides, she is gorgeous... Hum... Why not right? It doesn't mean anything, I can delight myself once, it doesn't mean anything, I won't damn my soul just because of that...<br /> Other demons simply may not care about corrupting that silly Mage at this moment... They have more pressing matters... &quot;So puny mortal, help me destroy the cults of Tarshkar, the unholy, lord of the flies of the seventh hell, who dares oppose my rule over the feud of the frozen wastelands, and I'll grant you what your heart desires!&quot;. Demons fight other demons even more than they fight any other, and they will happly use Mages as pawns in their conflicts.<br /> Smart demonologists will try to extract Intel about the many &quot;demonic cultures&quot;. In a sense, Demonology is actually a specific kind of &quot;sociology&quot;. Those Mages with a good amount of knowledge of the demonic courts and Realms, can play their rivalries for his benefit, being able to get many good bargains without losing his soul, or his free will.<br /> That's still a very dangerous endeavor, no matter what.<br /> As to what demons can offer, possibilities are huge. But, basically, Power. Knowledge. Influence. You name it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:44:31-08:00","id":1053374,"title":"","content":"<b>Summon Angels (Celestials)</b> Spirit 2<br /> Despite the name, those are not only the winged humans from abhraamic lore; the title of &quot;angels&quot; is the most common, but the right name of their category is &quot;Celestials&quot;. Those spirits from the High Umbra represent higher morals, positive emotions and things to aspire. Classic Christian archangels, Nordic Valkyries, greek Muses, servants from the chinese Celestial Bureoucracy and so.<br /> When first summoned, this kind of spirit will almost certanly answer. They'll be openly hostile only if the Mage is utterly currupt (like the Nefandi). Each type of Celestial values a different set of atributes: muses value love and beauty, valkyries value bravery and honor, angels value empathy and piety, archangels value courage and duty, celestial bureoucrats value order and sense of duty, and so on.<br /> Celestials will expect those seeking their services to live by their ideals; the Mage must be brave, must be humble, pious, must put the duty above his own personal wishes, must be charitable, live without vices, and many many more.<br /> As for favors, the most usual ones will be spreading the celestials values, protecting those they value, and fight off their demonic enemies. More than simply destroying terrible monsters with horns, that mostly means fighting what they represent - fight against hate, jeaulousy, cowardice, vice. Each celestial, usually also have one specific sin that they despise - valkyries hate cowardice, angels are anatema to hate, archangels despise lies, and so forth.<br /> Celestials are mostly helpful, but they expect the Mage to be able to deal with THEIR trials, rather than relying constantly on help. If the situation is dire, they won't refuse all the help they can handle, but they won't do all the job for the Mage. A Mage that cannot pull his weight may be pietyed, and, at best, the Celestials will send him to a purgatory-like realm, were he'll suffer, but will also be both safe and tought and made stronger. Celestials mostly use violence against the wicked, but a Mage that keeps summoning them for no good reason, may end up being cursed (losing all his money is a common thing).<br /> And, of course, if you are being persecuted for a demon, you can get a little help for free...<br /> Like the demons, the celestials have a tendency of atracting groups of cultists, that practice the so called &quot;White Magic&quot;. It is said that, the old Order of Reason Gabrielites were one such groups, the biggest know, found for the worship of the powerful archangels Gabriel. Needless to say, celestial cultists are the greatest enemies and nemesis of infernalists.<br /> Probably, the largest group of White Magic practicers are the Celestial Chorus, but Hermetics are also found of making alliances with this kind of spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:42:10-08:00","id":1053504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1051877#post1051877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 4--turn a candle into an explosive more powerful than a stick of dynamite. Probably most useful in earlier settings, but you can always carry candles with you in the modern age.<br /> <br /> Tallow and candle wax have several times more energy density than TNT. Unlike TNT, candles release that energy very slowly. But with Time 4, you can light a candle and cause it to release all its energy at once, by compressing its entire lifespan into an instant. Obviously Vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best part is, this is likely to be Coincidental. If someone lights a stick with a match, and it explodes soon after, any modern person would assume it was dynamite. Just, you know, painted to look like a candle. Or else some other kind of explosive, like C4 (I don't know if C4 explodes with fire, so it's a reasonable assumption that a HAB won't either).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:01:00-08:00","id":1053515,"title":"","content":"<b>Enhanced Paper Cut</b> - Matter 3<br /> <br /> By using the power to reshape materials - and, more importantly, to prevent them being reshaped - the user causes a piece of paper to resist bending, shearing, crumpling, or tearing. It will keep its shape, under stress, so long as the Duration lasts and those stresses are less than the Successes rolled for Structure. And since paper is thinner than most blades, it can serve as an effective and deadly cutting weapon. A simple playing card is like a knife, and far more easily carried or found without arousing suspicion. Using paper as a weapon may even be coincidental; paper cuts are a known phenomenon, though usually not deadly. Many industrious persons have turned paper into powerful weapons, however, and they didn't have recourse to magick.<br /> <br /> For this and other inventive control of paper, see <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Read_or_Die\" target=\"_blank\">Read Or Die</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:25:35-08:00","id":1053560,"title":"","content":"<b>Doppelganger</b> - Life 3, Mind 2<br /> Lets the Mage impersonate someone that he can see - both in the apareance as in the manners. The Mage will mimick every details about the target. The more successes, the better the disguise is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T19:44:08-08:00","id":1053593,"title":"","content":"<b>Dynamic Reading</b> Mind 3, Matter 1<br /> The Mage can absorb all the information contained on books, magazines, newspapers etc, just by touching them. All the letters in the paper are tranformed into processed thoughts inside the Mage's head. With this effect, a Mage can read a full library in a matter of minutes or hours.<br /> Technomancers can employ a similar effect, <b>Digital Reading</b>, using this to read things stored on computers, with Forces 1 instead of Matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-23-2017, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T00:23:01-08:00","id":1053681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1053593#post1053593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dynamic Reading</b> Mind 3, Entropy 3<br /> The Mage can absorb all the information contained on books, magazines, newspapers etc, just by touching them. All the letters in the paper are tranformed into processed thoughts inside the Mage's head. With this effect, a Mage can read a full library in a matter of minutes or hours.<br /> Technomancers can employ a similar effect, <b>Digital Reading</b>, using this to read things stored on computers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think Entropy should be replaced with Matter 1, since you otherwise don't know what all the papers say. Same with Forces 1 and digital mediums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:27:03-08:00","id":1053701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1053681#post1053681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think Entropy should be replaced with Matter 1, since you otherwise don't know what all the papers say. Same with Forces 1 and digital mediums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I guess you're right. Not to mention that it makes the effect easier. I'll fiz above","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:55:58-08:00","id":1053708,"title":"","content":"<b>Radio Sight</b> - Forces 1<br /> With this simple effect, the Mage can hear all radio frequencies around him. He can hear his favorite musics or watch TV directly inside his head.<br /> <br /> <b>Radio Telepathy</b> - Forces 2<br /> With this effect, the Mage can send sounds and images in the form of radio waves.<br /> <br /> Two Mages using both effects can effectively have a telephatic communication without the use of Mind, and even better, they can communicate over large distances without the need of Correspondence (you can thank the technocratic Consensus for that).<br /> However, despite all those obvious positive sides and easiness of access, this has the downside of letting anyone curious enough to hear the conversation. Maybe the Mages will wanna use some encrypting before using it.<br /> <br /> Make sure to use apropriate wave lenghts to adjust them to the desired distances<br /> <br /> Also, using a wave lenght previously combined makes the effect easier, effectively making giving the &quot;researched subject&quot; -1 dif modifier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-23-2017, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T03:43:46-08:00","id":1053741,"title":"","content":"<b>Microscopic Vision</b> - Correspondence 1<br /> Wanna see microbes with your naked eye? There you have it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T04:06:55-08:00","id":1053747,"title":"","content":"Hey, have any of you ever tough about using Level 1 Spheres for AGRESSIVE purposes? Well, take a look at that:<br /> <br /> <b>Reversed Vision</b> - Correspondence 1<br /> Make your target see things upside-down. That will make even his toughts harder. All rolls for the target will be at +4 dif, and the target will face extremly disorientation<br /> <br /> <b>Mirror Sight</b> - Spirit 1<br /> Make the target see the Penumbra or the Shadownlands of the Underworld, or both... Instead of the material world. Things will be very different there, which will cause massive disorientation (basically, many things in material world won't exist in the penumbra and vice versa, making the target bump into objects and walls. What's more, people and living beings in the material world may not be seen there, making those effectively invisible. It's debatable if the Mage, with an awakened avatar and etherial ressonance, could be seen in the penumbra).<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Noise</b> Mind 1<br /> Give the target the ability to sense psychic emanations... And, at the same time, amplify your own emanations to make a sort of &quot;psychic scream&quot;, causing massive disorientation (that's also pretty unpleasant). Increase all dif up to +3 for the target (so, 5 successes is enough to make that for a scene).<br /> <br /> <b>Energetic Sight</b> - Forces 1<br /> Make the target see several different energies - thermal vision, ultraviolet vision, radio hearing, x-ray sight, sound waves/vibration sight - all at once, and on top of his regular senses (each success gives the target one aditional sense). The sensorial overflow will cause confusion and disorientation; +1 dif on any rollsrolls for the first additional sense, +1 for every two other senses after that<br /> <br /> All those penalties are cumulative, so a target can be rendered useless by sensorial overflow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T05:05:43-08:00","id":1053759,"title":"","content":"Reversed Vision wouldn't be Corr 1. Arguably you couldn't do it on yourself either.<br /> <br /> It's a mind, life or forces effect, or even a combination of them. F2, L1 (for anchoring) should do it just fine.<br /> <br /> Check this trio (I've used them as an akashic style mage and as a combat cyborg style mage, refluff to taste)<br /> <b>Kinetic Redistribution</b> (Forces 2 or Forces 3) - Even better than protecting oneself in combat is to repurpose so much aggresiveness to your needs.<br /> Baseline, this magick gives you soak, and through the course of its effect you may store that energy (damage) for later use in combat.<br /> Half of the damage soaked may be spent on later damage effects to increase their damage on a 1:1 ratio.<br /> (to avoid explosiveness we capped how much could be transfered at once by your Forces sphere)<br /> With Forces 3 you may turn that damage into other types, kinetic into fire or electricity into cold, for example.<br /> As the effect expires you must dissipate that energy somehow. If you don't, you take the damage then, all at once (though it can be soaked normally).<br /> Usually just spending an action on the venting will do the trick. With F3 you can easily dissipate in multiple ways at once, being far safer though sometimes vulgar.<br /> <br /> <b>Seven Stars Advance</b> (Forces 2 or Forces 3) - This can be used as a damage spell or as an attack enhancer, I prefer the later.<br /> To the skilled fighter, being outnumbered is more cosmetic than problematic. Unmatched speed and accuracy allow you to strike multiple enemies with apparent ease.<br /> Successes determine how many people your attack roll will potentially hit. With Forces 2, damage is divided evenly before soak. With Forces 3 and an added source (a bit of quintessence, or damage stored from Kinetic Redistribution) your normal damage applies in full to each target.<br /> Restricting yourself to melee range usually makes this effect coincidental.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye of the Storm</b> (Forces 1, Mind 1) - To the skilled fighter, being outnumbered is more cosmetic than problematic!<br /> Reading your opponent is key to defending yourself. This magick is how you read every opponent at once.<br /> (Use this for denying outnumbered hindrances and then gain defense bonuses, life is good).<br /> Mulling on this effect, similar gains it can be made with Corr 1 Mind 1, or Time 2, or Life 2...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 02-23-2017, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T04:08:44-08:00","id":1054259,"title":"","content":"To deal with Wraiths<br /> <br /> <b>Feel the Chains of the Dead</b> - Mind 3, Spirit 1<br /> Allows the Mage to see the Passions and Dark Passions of a Wraith (or Specter).<br /> <br /> <b>A Feast of Feelings</b> - Mind 2<br /> Allows the Mage to generate the emotional influx that feeds of the Pathos (or Angst, as desired) of wraiths (if the Mage knows the emotion using the rote above)<br /> <br /> <b>Purge</b> - Mind 4, Spirit 2<br /> Removes temporary Angst from the wraith in a very painful way<br /> <br /> <b>Catalyse Psychy</b> - Mind 4, Spirit 2<br /> Temporarily remove the control of the shadown, if it's a wraith under catharsis or if it's a specter<br /> <br /> <b>Dead Juice</b> - Prime 3, Spirit 2<br /> Suck the Pathos of wraiths in the form of jhor filled quintessence<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Sinking</b> - Corr 3, Spirit 1<br /> Throw a wraith into the Tempest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:12:01-08:00","id":1054325,"title":"","content":"Mind Over Matter - Mind 1, Correspondence 1, Life 1, Forces 2<br /> <br /> The Mage meditates, and overrides their body's physical functions. Rather than control the physical by moving their body, the caster instead directly manipulates the motive forces created by their arm and directs them manually, overriding the normal restrictions of nerves, muscles and brain impulses and instead skipping directly from thought to result, manipulating their own physical form like a puppet.<br /> <br /> Three successes allows the caster to roll Meditation + Perception to take physical actions (climbing, jumping, combat, etc) instead of the normal Dexterity or Strength based dice pool. This effect lasts for the scene, or until the caster fails a roll, in which case their concentration is broken and the effect ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2149-isvan","name":"Isvan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T02:47:45-08:00","id":1054692,"title":"","content":"Mages and <i>The Dreaming</i>. Those effects require some special knowledge of the Mage about Faeries, so he MUST have the minimum amount of dots on the Lore (Faeries) knowledge skill (however, look up for the rote that allows Mages to copy skills to use, or let a spirit that has this knowledge possess you).<br /> <br /> <b>Enchant</b> - Mind 1, Spirit 1, Prime 2<br /> This rote <i>enchant</i> a person (the Mage himself or another) with the energies of the Glamour, allowing the enchanted person to see chimerical beings and objects and the fae mien of changellings.<br /> The needed spheres are debatable, and will be up to the ST: if the Dreaming zone is a mental Realm born of the subconscious of all dreamers, Mind 1 could suffice. If, however, the ST determines that it's a spiritual Realm, it would need Spirit 1. But the ST can say that it's a spiritual Realm born of the subconscious, and require both Mind 1 and Spirit 1. And finally, the ST may require that, to enchant someone, you need a point of Glamour, like in Changelling the Dreaming. In that case, the Mage will need Prime 2 and a quintessence point. The ST than may require any combination of Mind 1, Spirit 1, Prime 2, as he sees fit (I myself would require only Mind 1 OR Spirit 1 OR Prime 2 and 1 pt of Quint)<br /> The Mage must have at least 1 dot on Lore (Faeries) before he can learn this effect<br /> <br /> <b>Create Chimeras</b> - Mind 3, Prime 2<br /> The Mage can create an &quot;imaginary friend&quot;. Using Mind 3, the Mage can shape any Chimera he wishes. To &quot;give life&quot; to the dream however, it's a little more complicated... The Mage will have to spend quintessence to give it permanence... A lot of quintessence.<br /> If you're using the rules for creating chimeras, each Chimera Point that the Chimera have will need 1 point of quintessence and 1 success in this effect. (One Chimera point can buy 3 attributes, starting from 0, 3 skills, 1 permanent glamour. Willpower costs 3 chimera points, and the Redes, their powers that are similar to spirits charms, each one have a specific cost in chimera points).<br /> The Mage can create a VERY powerful chimerical spirit-like ally, he can even make it his personal totem or familiar, a spirit that can even manifest in the physical world or that can call the Wyrd (summon the Dreaming), at the cost of a huge amount of Quintessence.<br /> The best part of this rote is: this chimera is born out of the very ressonance of the Mage; it shares an simpathic link; it will even share the humor of the Mage, therefore it will <i>usually</i> be friendly to the Mage<br /> Optional rules: If the ST wishes to make this effect a little bit more challenging, he can request that the player use adequate quintessence in the form of Tass to give life to his Chimera; this would mean that he would need the adequate materials from the Dreaming itself. The way to acquire those, is by trading them with a changelling that can gather them, or by visiting the Dreaming itself and collect them. The Mage can just use quintessence in the form of Glamour directly instead, if he can make a Changelling (or another Chimera) to give him, or if the Mage manages to gather Glamour properly (I'll discuss a few options bellow).<br /> To use this effect, the Mage needs at least 4 dots in Lore (Faerie), and 5 dots if he wants to give his chimera the rare Rede of &quot;call the Wyrd&quot; (the most desired thing for any Mage using this power, as it gives him a mighty ally capable of fighting alongside the Mage in the material world)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-25-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:59:43-08:00","id":1054863,"title":"","content":"<b>Detect Trods</b> - Spirit 1<br /> The Mage can detect Trods with this effect (gates to the Dreaming)<br /> Need at least 1 dot in Lore (Faeries)<br /> <br /> <b>Open Trods</b> - Spirit 3<br /> The Mage can use a Trod to enter the Near Dreaming. Needs at least 2 dots in Lore (Faeries)<br /> <br /> <b>Dream Walk</b> - Mind 3<br /> The Mage can &quot;wake up in his dreams&quot;, jumping from his own dreams inside the Dreaming directly.<br /> This power allows the Mage to travel in the Dreaming in a pure mental form, similar to a simpler form of Astral travel.<br /> Theoretically, a Mage with enough knowledge of the Dreaming could find a Trod that leads to other spiritual Umbras, allowing him to travel to other spiritual realities with Mind 3 alone; that however, would be ridiculously hard and ridiculously dangerous to do. But, it can be done...<br /> The Mage doesn't need ANY knowledge of Faeries to use this effect, but doing this without knowing ANYTHING is a VERY stupid thing to do (unless you are VERY powerful, and even so, it's a risk business).<br /> If the Mage using this effect enters the Deep Dreaming or the Near Dreaming, it's up to the ST (I myself, would throw the player on the Deep Dreaming directly).<br /> With Mind 3,Correspondence 3, the Mage can travel in astral form to any place he knows of the Dreaming, if he has at least 3 dots in Lore (Fairie)<br /> <br /> <b>Dream Travel</b> - Spirit 3, Correspondence 3<br /> Enters the Dreaming directly, without the need of any Trods.<br /> The Mage can choose a familiar place of the Dreaming to go to, or, if this is the first time visiting this Realm, he will go to the closest area that ressambles his location in the material world in the Near Dreaming<br /> Need at least 3 dots in Lore (Fairies)<br /> <br /> <i>Note</i>: anyone that enters the Dreaming, becomes automatically enchanted while remains in the Realm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-25-2017, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:39:40-08:00","id":1054890,"title":"","content":"<b>Remove the Mists</b> - Mind 1<br /> Restore any memories numbed by the Mists, and protect against the powers of the Mists to erase the Mage's memories.<br /> Requires at least 1 dot in Lore (Fairies)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T23:49:33-08:00","id":1055111,"title":"","content":"<b>Lucky Weapon</b> - Entropy 3<br /> <br /> <b>Bind</b> - Correspondence 3<br /> Like a Ban, but inverted: it keeps the entity in place.<br /> <br /> <b>Constrict</b> - Matter 3<br /> Turns an enemy's clothes against them; their sleeves spontaneously weave into their sides or to each other, or something similar with their pants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:41:26-08:00","id":1057722,"title":"","content":"<b>Magnetic Overdrive-Kick</b> - Forces 2<br /> That one is... Well... See for yourselves...<br /> This effect is usually made permanent (because it isn't worthed to use it on the run, and because it can be VERY powerful). Basically, it will turn any mundane gun into a huge punch. If you use the optional rule of maximum amount of successes for ritual cast, which is Arete x Will, that means that most beggining chars will be capped at (3x5) 15 successes.<br /> So, take a mundane gun;<br /> -Spend 1 success to affect a target not yourself;<br /> -Give that gun 6 successes for this effect;<br /> -Now, spend 7 more successes to make it permanent (optional rule from <i>Revised</i> to make an effect permanent, double the required successes for duration).<br /> <br /> Now, your gun have a permanent 6 successes magnetic effect that speeds up ANY bullet that goes by the gun's barrel.<br /> <br /> RAW, Forces gives (success x2)+1 damage, but since your gun ISNT doing pure Forces damage, but rather just improving the damage it already does, I as an ST would give it 6 extra damage.<br /> <br /> So, there you have it, a peculiar kind of &quot;magikal&quot; item made without using Prime, but rather, with a permeffect.<br /> <br /> A simple pistol that could cause 4-7 damage per bullet, now will do 10-13... Pretty neat.<br /> <br /> Sons of <i>Ae</i>ther may place a few modifications on the barrel, adding tiny etherial magnetrons, VA could reprogram the ionic flux of the gun, hermetics will place mercurian runes and dreamspeakers would paint wind spirit gliphs in the weapon.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, use Prime 2 to enchant your bullets... Who needs Plasma guns anyway right?<br /> <br /> You may wanna put another permeffect on your gun to silence it... Because it will always be quite a Bang<br /> <br /> PS: if you can, buy Willpower 6 as soon as you can. That will allow you to place a permanent +8 damage to ANY fireweapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","user":"AgentSmith","date":". 03-03-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:48:00-08:00","id":1059046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1057722#post1057722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Magnetic Overdrive-Kick</b> - Forces 2<br /> That one is... Well... See for yourselves...<br /> This effect is usually made permanent (because it isn't worthed to use it on the run, and because it can be VERY powerful). Basically, it will turn any mundane gun into a huge punch. If you use the optional rule of maximum amount of successes for ritual cast, which is Arete x Will, that means that most beggining chars will be capped at (3x5) 15 successes.<br /> So, take a mundane gun;<br /> -Spend 1 success to affect a target not yourself;<br /> -Give that gun 6 successes for this effect;<br /> -Now, spend 7 more successes to make it permanent (optional rule from <i>Revised</i> to make an effect permanent, double the required successes for duration).<br /> <br /> Now, your gun have a permanent 6 successes magnetic effect that speeds up ANY bullet that goes by the gun's barrel.<br /> <br /> RAW, Forces gives (success x2)+1 damage, but since your gun ISNT doing pure Forces damage, but rather just improving the damage it already does, I as an ST would give it 6 extra damage.<br /> <br /> So, there you have it, a peculiar kind of &amp;quot;magikal&amp;quot; item made without using Prime, but rather, with a permeffect.<br /> <br /> A simple pistol that could cause 4-7 damage per bullet, now will do 10-13... Pretty neat.<br /> <br /> Sons of <i>Ae</i>ther may place a few modifications on the barrel, adding tiny etherial magnetrons, VA could reprogram the ionic flux of the gun, hermetics will place mercurian runes and dreamspeakers would paint wind spirit gliphs in the weapon.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, use Prime 2 to enchant your bullets... Who needs Plasma guns anyway right?<br /> <br /> You may wanna put another permeffect on your gun to silence it... Because it will always be quite a Bang<br /> <br /> PS: if you can, buy Willpower 6 as soon as you can. That will allow you to place a permanent +8 damage to ANY fireweapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice rote. I see you're following revised. Would M20 require Matter 2 to &quot;lock it&quot;?<br /> <br /> And what about adapting this in a sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:42:31-08:00","id":1059126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1059046#post1059046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice rote. I see you're following revised. Would M20 require Matter 2 to &quot;lock it&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, M20 would require Matter 2, at least according to RAW would seem; I've only bought my M20, Im still reading it, but nevertheless, I dont quite agree with that, so I houserule it out. But RAW according to M20, it would be Forces 2, Matter 2. For Revised, Forces 2 will do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049778-cheating-rotes?p=1059046#post1059046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what about adapting this in a sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, when I devised that rote, I was thinking A LOT about making it useful for swords too... In theory, its fair game.<br /> <br /> In practice thou... It may be problematic.<br /> <br /> This rote implies some kind of kinetic amplification. So... While this is great for bullets... Its not so good for swords... It would be easy to lose your balance if your sword moves much faster than you can control. Still, its not impossible, but probably it would impart some penalties to regain balance after each strike. Well... +2 maybe wouldn't cause trouble, after some practice, but anything beyond that would cause -1 dice to regain balance after each attack. Or, maybe this penalties could be offset with high amounts of strenght... I dont know.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, adding Entropy 2 to the effect would remove all penalties alltoghether<br /> <br /> So, here we go:<br /> <br /> <b>Magnetic Balanced Sword</b> - Forces 2, Entropy 2 (Matter 2, if you go with RAW M20)<br /> Each 2 successes beyond the two first gives a meele weapon a permanent bonus of +1 kinetic damage, without adding penalties to use the weapon, up to the maximum of +6 for initial chars (Arete x Willpower = maximum; 3 x 5 = 15; permanence = needed successes x2; 1 success per target, +6 for effect x 2 for permanence = 14)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","user":"AgentSmith","date":". 03-06-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}